1
00:06:02,399 --> 00:06:08,399
Cops or criminals. When you’re facing a loaded gun, what’s the difference?

2
00:12:04,799 --> 00:12:10,799
The Departed is a drama, thriller, crime film directed by Martin Scorsese.

3
00:18:07,199 --> 00:18:13,199
To take down South Boston's Irish Mafia, the police send in one of their own to
infiltrate the underworld, not realizing the syndicate has done likewise.

4
00:24:09,599 --> 00:24:15,599
While an undercover cop curries favor with the mob kingpin, a
career criminal rises through the police ranks.

5
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:18,000
But both sides soon discover there's a mole among them.

6
00:36:14,399 --> 00:36:20,399
Billy, played by Leonardo DiCaprio.

7
00:42:16,799 --> 00:42:22,799
Colin, played by Matt Damon.

8
00:48:19,199 --> 00:48:25,199
Costello, played by Jack Nicholson.

9
00:54:21,599 --> 00:54:27,599
Dignam, played by Mark Wahlberg.

10
01:00:24,000 --> 01:00:30,000
Queenan, played by Martin Sheen.

11
01:06:26,399 --> 01:06:32,399
Mr. French, played by Ray Winstone.

12
01:12:28,799 --> 01:12:34,799
The Departed is a 2006  crime thriller film directed by
Martin Scorsese and written by William Monahan.

13
01:18:31,199 --> 01:18:37,199
It is both an English-language remake of the 2002 Hong Kong film Infernal Affairs and also loosely based on the real-life Boston Winter Hill Gang; the character Colin Sullivan is based on
the corrupt Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) agent John Connolly, while the character Frank Costello is based on Irish-American gangster and crime boss Whitey Bulger.

14
01:24:33,599 --> 01:24:39,599
The film stars Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, and Mark Wahlberg, with Martin Sheen, Ray
Winstone, Vera Farmiga, Alec Baldwin, Anthony Anderson and James Badge Dale in supporting roles.

15
01:30:36,000 --> 01:30:42,000
The film takes place in Boston and the surrounding metro area,
primarily in the South Boston neighborhood.

16
01:36:38,399 --> 01:36:44,399
Irish Mob boss Frank Costello (Nicholson) plants Colin Sullivan (Damon) as a spy within the Massachusetts State Police;
simultaneously, the police assign undercover state trooper Billy Costigan (DiCaprio) to infiltrate Costello's mob crew.

17
01:42:40,799 --> 01:42:46,799
When both sides realize the situation, Sullivan and Costigan each attempt
to discover the other's identity before they are found out.

18
01:48:43,199 --> 01:48:49,199
The Departed premiered at the Ziegfeld Theatre on September 26, 2006
and was released on October 6, 2006 by Warner Bros.

19
01:54:45,599 --> 01:54:51,599
Pictures in the United States, with Media Asia
Distribution releasing in Hong Kong.

20
02:00:48,000 --> 02:00:54,000
The film was a critical and commercial success, grossing $291.5 million on a budget of around $90 million and receiving acclaim
for its direction, performances (particularly of DiCaprio, Nicholson, and Wahlberg), screenplay, and editing.

21
02:06:50,399 --> 02:06:56,399
It won several accolades, including four Oscars at the 79th Academy Awards: for Best Picture, Best Director for Scorsese (his only
personal Oscar win to date), Best Adapted Screenplay for Monahan, and Best Film Editing for editor Thelma Schoonmaker.

22
02:12:52,799 --> 02:12:58,799
The film also received six nominations each at the 64th Golden Globe Awards (winning one) and the 60th
British Academy Film Awards, and two nominations at the 13th Screen Actors Guild Awards.

23
02:18:55,199 --> 02:19:01,199
The film explores themes of police, undercover, boston,
massachusetts, gangster, irish-american.

24
02:24:57,599 --> 02:25:03,599
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and intense.
